# Frontend environment (Vite).
#
# The frontend no longer needs any Firebase configuration: authentication and all
# data now come from this project's own backend. Vite inlines VITE_* values at
# BUILD time, so a change here requires `npm run build`, not just a restart.

# Backend (Express + Socket.IO + Baileys) base URL.
#
# Leave EMPTY for:
#   - local development — Vite proxies /api and /socket.io to
#     http://localhost:5000 automatically
#   - single-origin deployment — the backend serves dist/ itself, so the frontend
#     calls /api on its own host (see deploy/DEPLOY-VPS-ONLY.md)
#
# Set it only when the frontend is hosted separately from the backend, e.g.
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com
VITE_API_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend configuration lives in the same .env file when the two run together.
# See deploy/.env.server.example for the full annotated list, and
# deploy/POSTGRES.md for database setup. The essentials:
#
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://wa_app:password@127.0.0.1:5432/wa_app
#   JWT_SECRET=<48+ random bytes; generate with the command in POSTGRES.md>
#   CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-domain
#   ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com
#
# The server refuses to start without DATABASE_URL and JWT_SECRET.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
